<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42256" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεθίζω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιζέμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.5
				</span></i>
			 : impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρέθιζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					965
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), 
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.419
				</span></i>
			 : fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					1.385
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mochl.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				13.4.2
			</span></i> : aor.1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρέθισα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					3.72
				</span></i>
			 ; poet. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					183
				</span></i>
			(lyr.), inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεθίξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.37
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>) : pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρέθικα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.37
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρεθίσθην,</span>
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεθισθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.40
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.57
			</span></i> : pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρέθισμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.), etc. : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέθω</span>):—<i>rouse to anger, rouse to fight,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.32
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερτομίοις ἐπέεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.419
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνας τ᾽ ἄνδρας τε,</span> of a
			lion, <i><span class="en">
				17.658
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοὺς Πέρσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.146
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλαύλους τ᾽ ἠρ. Μούσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					965
				</span></i>
			(lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ σφηκιὰν ἐ. τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					475
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖρον..ἐρεθίσαι γραῦν ἢ κύνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					802
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πὺξ ἐ.</span>
			<i>challenge to</i> a boxing-match, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.2
			</span></i> ; <i>provoke to curiosity,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητέρα σήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.45
				</span></i>
			 : generally, <i>excite, chafe,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένας ἐ. φόβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					183
				</span></i>
			(lyr.) ; of physical <i>irritation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mochl.</u>
				2
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆχες βραχέα -ουσαι</span>
			<i>causing</i> brief <i>irritation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				4.54
			</span></i> : metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πλανάτας χοροῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					148
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μάγαδιν</span>
			<i>to touch</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Telest.
				4
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλόγα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					8.9
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φονικὸν καὶ θηριῶδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.822c
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>incite</i> to rivalry, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be provoked, excited,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1104
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρεθισμένος</span>”
				<i>under provocation,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					574
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργῇ χεῖρασ-ισμένας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euphro
					8.3
				</span></i>
			 ; of love, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς νέοισιν -ισμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Timocl.
					30
				</span></i>
			 ; of fire, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέψαλος.. -όμενος..ῥιπίδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					669
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθὴρ -έσθω βροντῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1045
				</span></i>
			 (anap.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα
			ἠρεθισμένον,</span> of one who has run till he is out of
			breath, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1119
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκος ἠρεθισμένον</span>”
				<i>irritated,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.81.6
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσμὴ -ισμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					75.9
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν ὕβριν ἠρεθίσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> abs., <i>to
				be quarrelsome</i> or <i>perverse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.359
			</span></i>.</div>
